---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import car from '../../data/car.json';

const OCTOPUS_REFERRAL = 'https://share.octopus.energy/lush-spark-49';

const { use, annual_gbp: a, cost_per_mile_p: cpm, replaced, fuel_sensitivity: fs } = car;
const gbp = (n: number) => `£${Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-GB')}`;
const [qashqai, c4] = replaced.cars;

const allCosts = fs.rows.flatMap((r: any) => r.cost);
const lo = Math.min(...allCosts);
const hi = Math.max(...allCosts);
const shade = (v: number) => {
  const k = (v - lo) / (hi - lo);
  if (k > 0.72) return '#5b83e6';
  if (k > 0.45) return '#9ab4f2';
  if (k > 0.22) return '#c9d8f8';
  return '#e8eefc';
};
const ink = (v: number) => ((v - lo) / (hi - lo) > 0.72 ? '#fff' : 'inherit');

// pence per mile, scaled against the thirstiest thing we used to drive
const barMax = cpm.petrol_qashqai;
const bars = [
  { label: 'Enyaq · charged overnight at 7.6p', v: cpm.iog_night, tone: 'accent' },
  { label: 'Enyaq · from solar surplus, at the 12p we give up', v: cpm.solar_surplus_opportunity, tone: 'accent' },
  { label: 'Enyaq · on an ordinary flat tariff', v: cpm.standard_flat, tone: 'mid' },
  { label: 'Enyaq · charged at the day rate', v: cpm.day_rate, tone: 'mid' },
  { label: 'Citroen C4 · diesel', v: cpm.diesel_c4, tone: 'dark' },
  { label: 'Nissan Qashqai · petrol', v: cpm.petrol_qashqai, tone: 'dark' },
];
---

<Base
  title="The car"
  description="A Skoda Enyaq replacing a petrol Qashqai and a diesel Citroen C4. What 10,000 miles a year costs on an overnight tariff against petrol at 167p and diesel at 189p, and which part of the saving the solar can honestly claim."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>The car</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A <strong>Skoda Enyaq</strong> arrived in <strong>July 2026</strong> and is now the only car
      on the drive. It replaced two: a <strong>petrol Nissan Qashqai 1.6</strong> and a
      {' '}<strong>diesel Citroen C4</strong>, which had been splitting the mileage roughly half
      and half. It's the largest new electricity load this house has ever taken on, and at the same
      time one of the largest savings on the whole site. Those two facts are easy to confuse, so
      this page keeps them apart.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="note warn">
    <p><strong>Modelled, not measured.</strong> The car isn't metered separately from the house, so
    mileage, efficiency and charging losses here are estimates rather than readings. Both fuel
    figures use realistic real-world economy rather than manufacturer numbers, at UK average pump
    prices in September 2026. We'll swap in real figures after a full year of charging.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tiles" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Driven</p>
      <span class="figure md">{(use.miles_per_year / 1000).toFixed(0)}k<span class="unit">mi/yr</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">at {use.miles_per_kwh} mi/kWh</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Electricity used</p>
      <span class="figure md">{use.kwh_from_meter.toLocaleString('en-GB')}<span class="unit">kWh</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">off the meter, incl. charging losses</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Fuel it replaces</p>
      <span class="figure md">{gbp(a.fuel_baseline)}<span class="unit">/yr</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">two cars, blended {replaced.blended_pence_per_mile}p a mile</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Saving</p>
      <span class="figure md accent">{gbp(a.saving_total)}<span class="unit">/yr</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">{replaced.blended_pence_per_mile}p a mile down to {cpm.iog_night}p</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>What a mile costs</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    The Qashqai's 1.6 petrol managed about {qashqai.mpg_real} mpg in real use, which at
    {' '}{(qashqai.price_per_litre * 100).toFixed(0)}p a litre is
    {' '}<strong>{qashqai.pence_per_mile}p a mile</strong>. The C4 diesel was far more frugal at
    {' '}{c4.mpg_real} mpg, but diesel is the expensive pump now at
    {' '}{(c4.price_per_litre * 100).toFixed(0)}p, so it still cost
    {' '}<strong>{c4.pence_per_mile}p</strong>. The Enyaq, charged overnight, costs
    {' '}<strong>{cpm.iog_night}p</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="mile-bars">
      {bars.map((b) => (
        <div class="mrow">
          <span class="mlabel">{b.label}</span>
          <span class="mtrack">
            <span class={`mfill ${b.tone}`} style={`width:${(b.v / barMax) * 100}%`}></span>
          </span>
          <span class="mval">{b.v.toFixed(2)}p</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="caption">
      Pence per mile. Even charged at the worst possible moment, the middle of a weekday at the
      full day rate, the electric car is cheaper than the diesel was — and half the cost of the
      petrol.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Which part can the solar claim?</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    Almost none of it, and it matters that we say so. Most of this saving comes from the car being
    electric, not from the panels on the roof. Anyone with a driveway and a cheap overnight tariff
    gets the larger share of it without owning a single solar panel.
  </p>

  <div class="ledger">
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k">Petrol and diesel, two cars, 50/50</span>
      <span class="v">{gbp(a.fuel_baseline)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k">Same miles, electric, on an ordinary flat tariff</span>
      <span class="v">{gbp(a.ev_on_standard_flat)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k"><strong>Saved by going electric at all</strong></span>
      <span class="v"><strong>{gbp(a.saving_from_going_electric)}</strong></span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k">Same miles, charged in the overnight window</span>
      <span class="v">{gbp(a.ev_on_iog_night)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k"><strong>Saved again by the tariff</strong></span>
      <span class="v"><strong>{gbp(a.saving_from_the_tariff)}</strong></span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k"><strong>Total against the old fuel bill</strong></span>
      <span class="v"><strong>{gbp(a.saving_total)}</strong></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>This saving is deliberately kept out of the solar payback.</strong> The
    {' '}<a href="/stats/">payback tracker</a> measures the panels and the battery against what the
    same electricity would have cost without them. Folding {gbp(a.saving_total)} of avoided fuel
    into that number would make the solar look like it pays back in half the time, and it would be
    nonsense: we'd have saved most of it by buying the same car and plugging it into an ordinary
    house. Two separate good decisions, counted separately.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Fuel is the moving part</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    The electric side of this sum is fixed for twelve months. The pumps are not. Diesel is already
    near {(c4.price_per_litre * 100).toFixed(0)}p and creeping toward £2, and the old fuel bill
    rises with it while the charging bill doesn't.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>10,000 miles</th>
          {fs.scenarios.map((s: any) => <th>{s.label}</th>)}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {fs.rows.map((r: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{r.what.startsWith('Our') ? <strong>{r.what}</strong> : r.what}</td>
            {r.cost.map((v: number) => (
              <td style={`background:${shade(v)}; color:${ink(v)}; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:0.82rem`}>
                {gbp(v)}
              </td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="lede">
    Against {gbp(a.ev_on_iog_night)} of electricity, every square on that table is a saving of
    between {gbp(fs.rows[1].cost[0] - a.ev_on_iog_night)} and
    {' '}{gbp(fs.rows[0].cost[2] - a.ev_on_iog_night)} a year. The electric car doesn't need the
    pessimistic fuel forecast to win — it wins at today's prices and wins harder at tomorrow's.
  </p>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Charging it the wrong way round, on purpose</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    Right now the car charges from surplus solar on a granny lead, which looks like the obvious
    thing to do and is, for the moment, correct: export isn't being paid yet, so a spare kWh is
    worth nothing to anyone but us. Every unit that goes into the car instead of the grid saves the
    full import price.
  </p>

  <div class="note quiet">
    <p><strong>That flips the day export starts paying.</strong> Once the meter earns 12p for
    exported solar and the overnight rate is under 8p, the sensible move reverses: sell the
    sunshine, buy the cheap night power, and pocket the difference on every kWh the car takes. It
    feels wrong to stop charging a car from your own panels, which is exactly why it's worth
    writing down before the habit sets. See <a href="/tariff/">the tariff</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>The awkward bit</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    The car adds roughly {use.kwh_from_meter.toLocaleString('en-GB')} kWh a year to a house that
    generates about 9,900. In summer that's absorbed without noticing. In December it lands on top
    of a <a href="/heat-pump/">heat pump</a> in the same six-hour cheap window, and the battery,
    the car and the heating all want the same cheap hours. That's a scheduling problem rather than
    a cost problem, and it's Predbat's to solve. We'll publish how well it copes.
  </p>

  <div class="card referral" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
    <p class="kicker">Charging an EV at home?</p>
    <h2 style="margin:0.2rem 0 0"><img src="/octopus-mark.png" alt="" class="octopus-logo-inline" /> Octopus · we both get £50</h2>
    <p>The overnight rate is doing most of the work in the sums above. No sponsors on this site,
    and the referral pays you exactly what it pays us.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn octopus" href={OCTOPUS_REFERRAL} rel="noopener"><img src="/octopus-mark.png" alt="Octopus Energy" class="octopus-mark" /> Claim £50</a>
      <p class="fine mono">share.octopus.energy/lush-spark-49</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .mile-bars { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
    .mrow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 17rem 1fr 3.4rem; align-items: center; gap: 0.8rem; }
    .mlabel { font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .mtrack { background: var(--track); border-radius: 999px; height: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
    .mfill { display: block; height: 100%; border-radius: 999px; min-width: 6px; background: var(--dark); }
    .mfill.accent { background: var(--accent); }
    .mfill.mid { background: #9ab4f2; }
    .mval { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; text-align: right; color: var(--ink-400); }
    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .mrow { grid-template-columns: 1fr 3.4rem; }
      .mlabel { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin-bottom: -0.3rem; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
